From 5a7a148b035ff807e4cae7a13a5bd62296ddc3f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:20:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: T6050: hand the internal display over by default

The J714s DCP hand-off (chosen.asahi,t6050-display=1) has run at 3024x1890@120
with the GPU on two J714s: FatBoy721's (normal chain, lid sleep) and
TripleU613's (zink desktop, 6.9 W). Arm it by default; the hand-off's own
checks (DCP running, both DARTs locked on four-level ADT tables, a firmware it
can name) still leave simpledrm when anything is off, and
chosen.asahi,t6050-display=0 keeps the framebuffer on request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H3rUWsmTuAiei3A7JojjHG
